<title>UK: ANZ sets pricing on CESC $70 mln FRN.</title>
<headline>ANZ sets pricing on CESC $70 mln FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calcutta Electric Supply Corp Ltd (CESC) will launch a $70 million 10-year FRN on April 28, lead manager ANZ Investment Bank said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bond, maturing in May 2007, will be priced with a coupon of six-month Libor plus 150 basis points and a par issue price, the statement said.</p>
<p>CESC is the only distributor of electricity in Calcutta and will keep its exclusive distribution licence until at least 2020. Proceeds of the bond will be used to fund a $157 million project to expand CESC's network capacity.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
